Subject: [PATCH] kgsl: bracket trusted A3xx legacy shadow saves

The kernel-generated register/constant save IB reads HLSQ shadow RAM at
dword 0x6100 and related addresses. These overlap the protected SMMU address
window on Dior. Submit this internal IB through the existing PMODE bracket,
as the shader-save IB already does. User IB validation and protection ranges
are unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_a3xx.c b/drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_a3xx.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_a3xx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_a3xx.c
@@ -2424,9 +2424,15 @@ static int a3xx_drawctxt_save(struct adreno_device *adreno_dev,
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		/* save registers and constants. */
+		/*
+		 * This kernel-built IB saves HLSQ shadow RAM, including texture
+		 * objects at dword 0x6100 in the protected address window. Use
+		 * the trusted internal bracket, as shader_save does below; user
+		 * IBs retain protected mode before and after this submission.
+		 */
+		pr_info_once("Dior KGSL legacy shadow save: trusted PMODE bracket\n");
 		ret = adreno_ringbuffer_issuecmds(device, context,
-			KGSL_CMD_FLAGS_NONE,
+			KGSL_CMD_FLAGS_PMODE,
 			context->regconstant_save, 3);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
